; ============================================================================
;  undercover.sqs  -  disguise: establish cover, feed the native break, react.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Split of responsibilities with the native AlertMachine:
;    * gmUndercover is SCRIPT-OWNED. This file establishes cover at boot
;      (gmUndercover = true + setCaptive true, exactly as the old
;      escalation.sqs did) and drops it on a break. The engine only READS
;      the global each alert tick.
;    * The engine natively polls the vehicle-mount half of the break
;      ((vehicle aP) != aP) and spikes Heat on the nearest zone itself.
;    * The fired-weapon half stays scripted: a player "fired" event handler
;      calls gmBreakUndercover (latched, consumed by the next alert tick,
;      only effective while gmUndercover is true).
;    * On the native "undercoverBroken" event this manager un-captives the
;      player so occupiers re-acquire him (old alert.sqs break block; the
;      Heat spike that block also applied is native now).
;
;  EVENT-QUEUE CONSUMER: drains gmEvtUcBroken ([reason]).
;  OWNS: gmUndercover, gmEvtUcBroken (consumer), the player's fired-EH.
;  READS: gmWarLevel (escalation.sqs keeps gmUndercoverDetect updated).
;  Re-establishing cover after a break (disguise swap) stays a Phase-2 hook,
;  matching the old scripts: one break is permanent for the campaign.
; ============================================================================
@GM_LIB_READY

; ---- establish the breakable cover ONCE at boot ------------------------------
gmUndercover = true
aP setCaptive true
gmUndercoverDetect = gmWarLevel / 10

; fired-weapon break trigger. NOTE: deliberately NOT a "carries a weapon" test -
; the guerrilla is always armed; only actually firing blows the disguise.
aP addEventHandler ["fired", {gmBreakUndercover "fired"}]

; ============================================================================
;  MAIN LOOP - consume the native break event
; ============================================================================
#loop
~2
? (count gmEvtUcBroken) < 1 : goto "loop"
GM_uBatch = gmEvtUcBroken + []; gmEvtUcBroken = []
gmUndercover = false
aP setCaptive false
hint "Cover blown - the occupiers are onto you."
goto "loop"
